# Rules Map (Index-First Routing)

**Do not load every file in this directory into context.**  
`../AGENTS.md` is the universal always-on entry point for all harnesses. It **points** at rules. Load a rule body only when its trigger fires or you must enforce a gate.

## Always-Active (Pointers in AGENTS.md / Instructions)

These rules are referenced from the always-loaded instruction files. Load the rule body when you encounter the trigger condition.

| Rule | Trigger | Size |
|---|---|---|
| `authority.md` | Decision ownership, operating mode selection, elevated autonomy, process/resource safety, material decisions | small |
| `evidence.md` | Verification, self-review, "done" claims, side-effect tool calls, user skepticism or pushback | small |
| `skill-use.md` | Discovering a skill (index-first) or after selecting a skill (binding workflow commitment) | small |
| `execution-safety.md` | Before the first shell command in every session; every command thereafter, sandbox routing, secrets, long-running processes | small |
| `git-safety.md` | Git staging, committing, pushing, or destructive git operations | small |
| `code-quality.md` | Code implementation, capability reuse, test persistence and existing domain vocabulary | small |

## On-Demand (Load When Trigger Fires)

| Rule | Trigger | Size |
|---|---|---|
| `document-formats.md` | Creating, saving, substantially revising, or sharing human-facing documents; choosing report/specification formats | small |

## Layering & One-Way Boundary

```
AGENTS.md / instructions (always) → rule pointer → rule body (on fire)
                                  → skills/INDEX → SKILL.md → references/*
```

**One-way boundary:** Rules may reference skills and skill references for domain workflows. Skills must **never** depend on or link back to rule files.

## Anti-patterns

- Bulk-reading `rules/*.md` at session start — load only when triggered
- Modifying `.agents/`, skills, or rules without loading `skill-author` and checking https://agentskills.io + https://agents.md
- Duplicating rule text into skills or creating rule dependencies inside skills
- Loading skills without checking `skills/INDEX` first
